==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|favourable}}, from {{der|en|fro|favorable}}, from {{der|en|la|favōrābilis}}, from {{m|la|favor}}. {{surf|en|favor|-able}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfeɪvəɹəbəl/|[ˈfeɪvɹəbɫ̩]|a=RP,GA,CA}}
** {{audio|en|En-us-favorable.ogg|a=California}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfæɪvəɹəbəl/|[ˈfæɪvɹəbɫ̩]|a=AU}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfæɪvəɹəbəl/|[ˈfæɪvɹəbɫ̩]|[ˈfæɪvɹəbʊ]|a=NZ|q2=cultivated}}
* {{hyph|en|fav|or|able}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{standard spelling of|en|favourable|from=US}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1871|author=Ohio State Medical Society|title=Transactions of the Annual Meeting|page=135
|passage=The conditions '''favorable''' to health and life of the indigines of the poles or the north temperate zones are destructive to the indigines of the tropical, and vice versa.}}

